WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.410
The oceans hold 96.54 per
cent of all Earth's water.

2
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.270
Ice caps, glaciers and permanent
snow hold 1.74 per cent.

3
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.190
Groundwater, 1.69.

4
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.590
And the atmosphere?

5
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.590
Just 0.001 per cent.

6
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.990
On this chart, it is too thin to see.

7
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.390
So how does such a tiny
store keep the rain falling?

8
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:27.510
Are clouds huge stores
that last for years?

9
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.500
Is new water made up there?

10
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.610
In this mission, you'll measure
Earth's four water stores,

11
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.430
and find out where the fresh water is.

12
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.110
Then you'll follow air as it
rises, cools and forms cloud,

13
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.870
and track change from a
hillslope to an ice age.

14
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:47.390
Your mission: explain how a store
this small keeps the rain falling.
